      "provenance": "literature_retrieved",
      "rationale": "The signal peptide of human MXRA8 spans residues 1\u201319 (landmark-authoritative); the mature extracellular N-terminus begins at residue 20 (V). A tag placed 'downstream of the signal peptide' therefore inserts after residue 19 (A), the sole extracellular N-terminal junction \u2014 no other reading is possible. Python confirmed residue_before = A (pos 19) and residue_after = V (pos 20). L3 provides the strongest validation: the N-terminal tag did not diminish CHIKV infection, demonstrating both surface display and preserved receptor function. L2 (PMC7163869): An N-terminal tag placed downstream of the signal peptide was used across Mxra8 orthologs to confirm surface expression by antibody staining. L3 (same paper) reports the functional test specifically on mouse Mxra8 bearing this N-terminal tag.",
